  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-03-24T04:22:25.247Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "All of this is mostly to help streamers and youtubers since I notice they tend to run into a little trouble when it comes to traveling between words with a large group of people. Honestly, I feel like this might be in the works already, and I've seen requests for similar features, but I couldn't find anything exactly the same so I thought I would just put in here.\n\nA Party would be a temporary group of players that could either be formed while in a world with anyone in the room by clicking on a player or selecting them in the social tab, like when you make friend requests, or with friends that may be in separate worlds through the social tab (ideally you would be able to talk with party members in other worlds, but I don't know how easy that would be to add in). \nYou could have a private mode option to have the party be mute to everyone else/ have everyone else be mute for the party. \nYou could also have a \"call\" mode that lets everyone in the party hear each other no matter how far apart they are.\nParty members would have the ability to send invites to the entire group at once instead of one at a time.\nWhen someone outside of the party is inviting a party member to a world the game could display a message saying \"This player is in a party would you like to invite their party?\" and maybe include details like how many people are in the party and whether the party is in private mode etc. and then give them the option to either invite the party, invite only the one player, or not invite anyone. \nYou could also have party information appear on the friends page when you select them in the social tab. (you could also add a \"do not disturb/afk\" option to the social tab so you can tell your friends that you are online, but not available at the moment. Since I'm pretty sure there isn't one yet.)\nYou actually might need to add a party tab in the menu so you can quickly see who is in your party, who the party leader is,  a \"kick/vote kick from party\" option when you don't want someone in your party, a \"disband\" option to remove everyone from the party, and a \"leave party\" button. The party leader could have an \"invite party to current world\" button here as well.\nIf a party leader tries to add someone to their party that is already in a party they could send a party merge request to the other party leader.(it occurs to me that it would be hard to say who the leader of a merged party should be and this also raises the question how big a party can get. i would guess most parties would be about 4-10 people, but there would probably be some rare  cases where 20-30+ people are in a group)\nParty leaders should also have the option to make another player the leader.",
